{% extends 'site/guideBase.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}
    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Regions</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>
                Regions are the building blocks of your empire. Click on any of your regions on the
                <a href="{{ url('Guide/World') }}">world map</a> to view and manage it.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Region Details</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>Each region has the following properties:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>Coordinates (X, Y):</b> The region's position on the hex map.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Terrain type:</b> Determines what can be built. Land regions (grassland, forest, hills, mountain) support standard buildings and units. Coastal and water regions (sand, shallow water, water, deep water) allow harbors and naval units.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Building space:</b> Each region has a maximum of 1000 building space. Buildings and units take up space, so you need to manage it carefully. For example, if a region shows 400/1000, you have used 400 space and can build 600 more.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Stationed units:</b> The military units currently garrisoned in this region, organized by category (Troops, Air Units, Naval Units, etc.).
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Expanding Your Empire</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>
                You can acquire new regions in two ways:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Buy:</b> Click on an unowned region on the map to purchase it. The cost increases with each region you already own.</li>
                <li><b>Conquer:</b> <a href="{{ url('Guide/Attack') }}">Attack</a> an enemy region and win the battle to capture it.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
